{
  "id": "ss.relic.blackspore",
  "name": "Black spore",
  "description": "ss.relic.luck gone wrong: the same four caps on the same tilted stem, at the same places and sizes, but the caps are dusky dark instead of green, the stem is ash grey, each cap carries a violet rim of light along its lower edge as if lit from beneath by the ruins' curse, and the one crown still lit is the bottom-right — the cap that in the green one has no crown at all — in arcane, with two motes lifting off it. Fifty more luck for two more curse is the four-leaf with the price showing, so the composition is copied exactly and only the light changes. The rims are crescents and not full rings, because a dark disc inside a bright ring is an eye, four times over.",
